    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2502.01621v1</id>
    <title>UV Radiation Measurement of Nitrogen in shock focusing facility</title>
    <updated>2025-02-03T18:52:33Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.01621v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2502.01621v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>A study on UV radiation in shock focused gas has been carried out in high temperature radiating Air experimentally. Spherical shock wave focusing was achieved with the help of a contoured converging section attached to a shock tube. The measured radiation is compared with SPECAIR software to find out that the radiation corresponds to the emission of N2+ Meinal transition. The temperature of the radiating gas was estimated from SPECAIR and was found to be around 6000K.</summary>
